    By default, ``jnp.nanmin`` computes the minimum of elements along the flattened
    array.

    >>> nan = jnp.nan
    >>> x = jnp.array([[1, nan, 4, 5],
    ...                [nan, -2, nan, -4],
    ...                [2, 1, 3, nan]])
    >>> jnp.nanmin(x)
